WEBVTT

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.860
Excuse me.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.720
What's wrong?

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.970
Did something happen?

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:29.110
What's going on?

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.230
His pulse stopped.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.400
He's had a heart attack.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.610
A heart attack?

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.240
That's impossible...

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.490
He's dead?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.200
Unfortunately, there's nothing else I can do here.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.490
What?

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.750
Call the captain!

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.620
Right!

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.750
What's wrong?

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.710
It seems somebody had a heart attack...

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.500
It looks like it's too late for them.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.550
How unfortunate.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.800
Boss, wake up!

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.180
Impossible!

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:27.120
Splendid as always, Eva.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:33.290
There are many professional killers, but only a handful can truly be called "the best."

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.550
Not only do you leave no proof, you also leave no evidence to say that it was even a murder.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.050
You're the only one with that technique.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.720
But that may prove to be to your disadvantage.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.560
The New York Mafia is searching for you.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:54.070
They've obtained information that you were the only person who could have done that killing.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.570
I'm honored to hear that even the New York Mafia knows my name.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.070
Eva...

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.410
Until things calm down, you should go into hiding.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.580
There's no need for that.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.160
If there was a professional capable of killing me...

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.580
It wouldn't matter where I hide.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.460
You're saying that there's no such person?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.380
You're very confident, Eva.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:21.930
Next time I get a job, maybe I'll have them raise the pay.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.270
Looking at you brings back memories of a certain man.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.230
He's just like you, a professional killer.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:36.400
He did his work unaffected by emotion, almost like a machine.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.110
Golgo 13.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.900
That was his name...

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.330
Do you know him?

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.620
No, but I've heard the name.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.170
Somehow, he's like you.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.880
He has the same scent.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:13.350
GOLGO 13

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:23.200
hissori to iki wo hisome machitsudzuketa kokoro tada kakimushirinagara

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:23.200
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:34.540
ippun ichibyou ga konna ni mo nagaku kanjiru koto ha nakatta

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:34.540
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:46.300
sora wo miage kaze ni koikakeru ima boku ha Oh tobidaseru ka

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:46.300
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:52.600
kako no yowai jibun ha mou inai

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:52.600
The weak person I was is no more

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:58.190
tada shinjiru koto ni kimeta

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:58.190
I decided to just believe

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.320
egaita yume wo ima kono te ni shite

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.320
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.160
kimi no hou he

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.160
I go towards you

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.870
kowarete kanjita kono omoi se ni shite

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:16.870
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.000
kimi no hou he

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.000
I go towards you

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.050
kaze ni fukarete

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.050
Blown by the wind

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.510
ohh fukarete

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:30.510
Oh blown

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:38.440
Eva, Heading for the Sea

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.700
I never thought that she was an assassin.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.500
They say that beautiful women have thorns,

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.000
but I never thought that I'd see one who could turn a single needle into a lethal weapon.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.380
She's an ace killer.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.500
If we're going to take out such a fearsome woman...

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:06.170
So the only one who can do it is Golgo 13?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.300
I don't care how much it costs.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.390
The bosses have all agreed to hire Golgo 13.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:18.270
None of them will be able to sleep until she's been taken out.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.200
He doesn't seem to be here yet...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.160
I don't see his car.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.790
I've heard he's very strict about time, but there's still 10 minutes.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:43.710
Want to grab a smoke?

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.550
I'm ready whenever.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.180
Golgo 13!

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.470
You were already here?

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.020
We thought you weren't here because your car isn't here.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.860
Where is it?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.190
It doesn't matter.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.320
Let's talk about work.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.200
Then...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.320
First, look at this picture...

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.040
Slowly.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.330
This is the target.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.210
Eva Krueger.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.010
Do you know her?

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.010
No.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.390
Keep talking.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.920
So, it is you.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:11.470
Hello.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.970
I never thought we'd meet again.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.470
Here you are.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.350
To celebrate our meeting.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.770
How many years has it been?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.730
Three years and six months.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.900
Thanks.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:36.120
You always remembered me, didn't you?

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.410
Yes...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:42.080
It's been three years, six months, and fifteen days to be exact.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.780
A gimlet.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.910
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.740
Here you are.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.950
Thanks.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.130
What?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:12.750
A time bomb?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:16.590
Yes, I just heard the crew talking.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.550
They were all in a panic.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.140
If that's true, then we're in trouble!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.010
What's wrong?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.470
Did something happen?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.600
A bomb might be planted onboard this ship.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.190
What?

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:34.360
Anyway, we need to go to the captain and ask him.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.440
Yes.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.650
Let's go, everyone.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.990
Wait a second.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:48.580
They said a bomb might be planted on this ship.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:49.710
Yeah.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.130
You won't go to captain's room with everyone else?

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.630
I'm sorry.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.680
Panicking won't help.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.550
And you?

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.930
I'm the same...

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.600
We're in the middle of the stormy ocean.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.560
What will happen, will happen.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.240
Everyone, listen, please.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:29.250
We received an emergency message from the Lisbon police.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.710
According to them, a passenger who departed this ship in Lisbon

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.840
told them that he planted a time bomb onboard.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.590
I knew it...

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:43.300
Everyone, remain calm.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:47.390
We still don't know if it's true or if it is just a prank.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.520
The Lisbon police are still investigating,

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:53.560
and until we receive additional word, we're going to perform a thorough search of the ship.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.810
Everyone, please help us.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.440
We don't have time for that!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:01.700
What if it goes off while you're searching?

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:02.660
That's right.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.490
You should put the safety of the passengers first.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:08.580
Is there no place onboard the ship that's absolutely safe?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.580
First, give us instructions and a place to evacuate to.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.830
Excuse me.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:21.420
Captain, according to the Lisbon police, the man who was thought to have planted the bomb committed suicide.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.050
What?

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.550
And the bomb?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.680
They still don't know,

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:32.560
but the man was a member of the Yorkshire terrorists who were behind the London bombings.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.350
He was a terrorist?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.690
There's no doubt about it.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.980
There's no doubt about it.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.530
The ship will sink!

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:42.990
What should we do?

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:44.610
The lifeboats!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.620
We should escape the ship via the lifeboats!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.490
That's right, the lifeboats!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.490
Everyone, calm down.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.500
Don't be stupid!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.420
The bomb will go off any second and sink the ship!

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:55.750
How can we be calm?!

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.750
We're in the middle of a storm!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.630
It's dangerous to lower the boats!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.800
Hurry, lower the boats!

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.050
Everyone, please wait!

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.790
Search the ship.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:40.840
Find the bomb as soon as you can.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:40.840
Go!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.750
Right!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.850
You aren't leaving?

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:58.850
There's very little difference between remaining in a ship with a bomb onboard and rowing a lifeboat in stormy seas.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:01.520
I think so too.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:06.110
Both of those choices are equally dangerous.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.490
You look over there!

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:11.450
Right!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:17.750
Shall we at least help with the search as well?

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.000
They found it! They found it!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:20.830
Really?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.960
They found something that looks like a bomb in Passenger Block B.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:26.590
Let's go!

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.010
Okay.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.360
This is it, captain!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.450
Is there anyone here who knows how to diffuse a bomb?

00:14:55.450 --> 00:15:00.420
If we try it without knowing what we're doing, it may blow up prematurely.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.290
But if we don't hurry...

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.790
Even as we stand here...

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.170
May I try?

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.890
Excuse me, have you ever disarmed a bomb before?

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.110
No.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.490
10 minutes.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.160
We have to try.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.530
But...

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.870
Everyone, leave.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.700
Understood.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:38.870
We're counting on you.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.840
Why don't you leave?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.720
I thought that if you failed,

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:59.390
you'd be lonely without at least one person to go with you.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:41.980
Captain.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.560
There's only 2 minutes left...

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:57.870
What happened?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.120
It's okay now.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:01.830
Really?

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.460
It's stopped!

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.880
He disarmed it!

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.510
Sound the horn!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:15.590
We'll save the people who left on the boats.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.430
Okay.

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:28.110
In the past, I've never met a man who had the same scent as mine.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:14.280
The sound of that horn remains in my ears...

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.580
Two people of the same type...

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.330
We never did ask each other's name.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:39.180
But I was happy to run into you by chance.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:40.970
No.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.180
It wasn't by chance.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.320
Goodbye, Eva.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.120
He knew my name...

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.800
Goodbye, my love.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.550
Goodbye, Golgo 13.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.350
You want to take a break from work?

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:29.270
Yes.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.150
That's fine, but what's happened?

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:34.730
Did something happen to you?

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:35.690
No.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:37.780
I only hope that's true...

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.490
I don't think that "cancellation fee" is the best word for it,

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.620
but this is my thanks for taking care of me so far.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:47.870
Take it.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:49.960
Eva...

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.750
I'll be going now.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.380
Wait.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.010
Do you intend to quit this line of work?

00:20:01.430 --> 00:20:02.130
Goodbye.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.190
Oh my...

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:04.200
Hey, that girl is...

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.500
Eva?

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.080
Yes, isn't that Eva?

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:33.350
You...

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.140
It's been a while.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.310
Eva, how many years has it been?

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.360
You've come back to the island?

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.150
I just stopped here for a while.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:45.150
I'll be leaving again soon.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.860
To a far away place...

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.370
I see.

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:39.000
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.500
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:53.430
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.720
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:03.820
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.650
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:12.950
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:21.250
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.800
It was just a dream

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.170
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:34.220
In this calm night

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.390
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:41.520
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:47.530
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:54.030
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.920
The detective's fiancée, a female detective,

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:08.800
was killed by the masked man, Michael.

00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:12.550
To take revenge, he asks Golgo to assassinate Michael.

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:15.300
Golgo attacks his hideout alone, but...

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:19.310
The shadow of the god of death approaches the man who works miracles...

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.980
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:25.940
The Saint Who Smelled of Death

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:23.730
The Saint Who Smelled of Death.

00:24:24.270 --> 00:24:28.190
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
